# OpenPlan monorepo-level local artifacts

# Local agent orchestration output. Durable work from these lanes is merged by
# cherry-picking reviewed commits, not by versioning worktree/log directories.
.agent-logs/
openplan-worktrees/

# Generated local story-pack artifacts (non-canonical)
openplan/.artifacts/

# Playwright MCP browser session logs and page snapshots. Written into the repo
# root by the MCP browser tools during local debugging; they are per-session
# scratch, not evidence, and accumulate megabytes if left untracked.
.playwright-mcp/

# Supabase CLI local temp metadata
openplan/supabase/.temp/

# Repository-local fallback when the system /tmp quota is exhausted.
/.tmp/

# Root-level node_modules. `openplan/.gitignore` covers the app's own copy, but the
# monorepo root had no rule, so vitest's cache file (.vite/vitest/**/results.json)
# was committed and re-dirtied the tree after every test run.
/node_modules/

# Local env snapshots
*.env.local.backup
.operator-private/
.vercel
.venv
.venv*/
__pycache__
data/pilot-nevada-county/.venv/
data/pilot-nevada-county/*.zip
data/pilot-nevada-county/roads/
data/pilot-nevada-county/tracts/
data/pilot-nevada-county/*.csv.gz
data/pilot-nevada-county/aeq_project/
data/pilot-nevada-county/run_output/*.omx
data/pilot-nevada-county/run_output/state_*.json
data/pilot-nevada-county/caltrans_2023_aadt.xlsx
data/pilot-nevada-county/run_output_v2/
data/pilot-nevada-county/run_output_v3/
data/pilot-nevada-county/validation/rerun_*/
data/pilot-nevada-county/runs/

# Superseded county-specific Placer pilot scratch/runtime artifacts
# Keep the tracked validation scaffolds; park the exploratory county-local build assets.
data/pilot-placer-county/aeq_project/
data/pilot-placer-county/package/
data/pilot-placer-county/roads/
data/pilot-placer-county/run_output/
data/pilot-placer-county/tracts/
data/pilot-placer-county/*.csv.gz
data/pilot-placer-county/build_network_package.py
data/pilot-placer-county/build_trip_tables.py
data/pilot-placer-county/step1_osm.py
data/pilot-placer-county/step2_assign.py

# Local screening-run experiments and transfer artifacts not selected as canonical repo truth
# Existing tracked run bundles remain versioned; these rules only park current local leftovers.
data/screening-runs/grass-valley-core-generic-v1/
data/screening-runs/nevada-county-runtime-diagnostics-20260324/
data/screening-runs/nevada-county-runtime-extscalar05-20260324/
data/screening-runs/nevada-county-runtime-mainline-scalar0369-diagnostics-20260324/
data/screening-runs/nevada-county-runtime-norenumber-20260324/
data/screening-runs/nevada-county-runtime-purposemix-a-20260324/
data/screening-runs/nevada-county-runtime-validation-20260324-remapfix/
data/screening-runs/placer-county-runtime-connectorbias2-20260324/

# Cached LODES WAC downloads for the AequilibraE worker (regenerated on demand)
workers/aequilibrae_worker/.lodes_cache/

# Where a screening run actually lands. `screening_runtime` defaults to these
# two paths under the repo root, so anyone who runs a model — including the
# modeling worker container, which bind-mounts the checkout — writes hundreds
# of megabytes of OSM extracts, TIGER downloads and matrices straight into
# their working tree. The individually-listed run directories above predate
# this rule and stay listed; the tracked reference bundle under
# data/screening-runs/ is unaffected, because ignore rules never apply to a
# file git is already tracking.
data/screening-runs/
data/_screening_cache/
data/activitysim-bundles/
qa-harness/output/
workers/aequilibrae_worker/data/gtfs/.gtfs_cache/

# The agreement study's per-county artifacts — ActivitySim outputs, bundles,
# demand packages and comparison JSON, several gigabytes per batch. The
# registry itself IS tracked and must stay so: that commit is the study's
# pre-registration, and it is the one file here that is evidence rather than
# output.
data/agreement-study/runs/

# Gateway study execution logs contain full model subprocess output and can be
# hundreds of megabytes. The small status, hashes, summaries and dated findings
# beside them remain tracked evidence.
data/modeling/gateway-volume-study-2026-08-22/runs/*/*/logs/

# Frozen development-validation source bytes, network databases, and model
# workspaces are multi-gigabyte local custody artifacts. Keep their compact
# readiness manifest, assessments, hashes, and dated report tracked beside
# this rule; those are the reproducible release evidence.
data/modeling/development-validation-study-2026-08-28/instruments/
data/modeling/development-validation-study-2026-08-28/runs/
data/modeling/development-validation-study-2026-08-28/shared-sources/

# Worker job manifests (`tmp/county-onramp/<run>.manifest.json`) — a transcript
# of one local run, regenerated every time.
/tmp/

# Personal Claude Code preferences (private, not shared)
CLAUDE.local.md

# generated test-output artifacts — never version these
docs/ops/*-test-output/

# Local Python venv (dir in the main checkout; symlink in worktrees) — never track
workers/aequilibrae_worker/.venv311

# Agent-session working files are local to this machine. Root AGENTS.md and
# CLAUDE.md became tracked eight-line shims on 2026-08-25 so every clone reaches
# the shared public operating manual; detailed personal instructions remain in
# each harness's ignored global file.
# These patterns are deliberately UNANCHORED: they match at every directory
# depth, because owner tooling config is local-only wherever it lives (the
# 2026-08-03 sweep missed the nested openplan/.mcp.json exactly because only
# the root copy was considered). If a nested file by one of these names ever
# genuinely belongs in the repo, that is a deliberate decision — use
# `git add -f` and record why.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md
.playwright-mcp/
.mcp.json
opencode.json
